#___________________________________________________________________
#
# File: c_ss2.dat
#
# Description: Data file used by c_wizard.cgi to run the solar system
#	trivia game.  Called from c_ss.html

# The following data is used to set the environment variables for the
#   question and answer pages generated by the CGI program.  This information
#   is specific to each category.
#
# ENVIRONMENT         Indicates the start of the environment data.
# BACKGROUND COLOR=   Set this if no background image is used.  Otherwise "".
# BACKGROUND IMAGE=   The background image.  Set to "" if not used.
# TEXT COLOR=         The color of the text.
# COVERPAGE ICON=     The icon used to return to the cover page.
# COVERPAGE FILENAME= The coverpage file name.
# CATEGORY FILENAME=  The main category file name such as the zoo or school 
#                       page. 
# CATEGORY ICON=      The icon for returning to the main category page.
# CATEGORY TEXT=      The test to go with the category icon.
#______________________________________________________________________

ENVIRONMENT
BACKGROUND COLOR="#000000"
BACKGROUND IMAGE=""
TEXT COLOR="#ffffff"
COVERPAGE ICON="ss_icon.gif"
COVERPAGE FILENAME="c_ss.html"
HELP FILENAME="c_sshlp.html"
CATAGORY FILENAME="school.html";
CATAGORY ICON="retschool.gif"
CATAGORY TEXT="Return to School"

#______________The records begin here__________________

.
QUESTION	Which of these contains 99.85% of all the matter in the Solar System?
INCORRECT_ANS1	Earth accounts for a very small portion of total mass of the Solar System.
IMG1	c_ear1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS2	Venus accounts for a tiny portion of the total mass of the Solar System.
IMG2	c_ven1.gif
CORRECT_ANS	The Sun accounts for 99.85% of all the matter in the Solar System.  The planets only contain 0.135% of the total mass.
IMG3	c_sun1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS3	Although a large planet, Saturn accounts for a very small portion of the total mass of the Solar System.
IMG4	c_sat3.gif
.
QUESTION	Our Solar System resides in a spiral galaxy consisting of 200 billion stars called:
INCORRECT_ANS1	Jupiter is a planet in our Solar System.
IMG1	c_jup1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS2	Venus is a planet in our Solar System.
IMG2	c_ven1.gif
CORRECT_ANS	The Milky Way Galaxy is the home of our Solar System.
IMG3	c_mil1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS3	Saturn is a planet in our Solar System.
IMG4	c_sat3.gif
.
QUESTION	Because of its highly elliptical orbit, this planet is actually closer to the Sun than is Neptune during portions of its orbit.
INCORRECT_ANS1	You chose Earth.  Earth is the third planet from the Sun and always closer to the Sun than Neptune.
IMG1	c_ear1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS2	Close, but Uranus is always closer than Neptune to the Sun.
IMG2	c_ura1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS3	You chose the Sun itself.
IMG3	c_sun1.gif
CORRECT_ANS	Because of its irregular orbit Pluto is actually closer, at times, to the Sun than is Neptune.
IMG4	c_plu1.gif
.
QUESTION	Terrestrial Planets are the four innermost planets in the Solar System.  Which planet is a Terrestrial Planet?
CORRECT_ANS	Mercury is considered a Terrestrial Planet because it is one of the four innermost planets.  They are called Terrestrial because they are compact and rocky like the Earth's surface.
IMG1	c_mer1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS1	Jupiter is a Jovian Planet because of its gaseous nature.
IMG2	c_jup1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS2	A comet is not one of the four innermost planets.
IMG3	c_hai1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS3	Saturn is a Jovian Planet because of its gaseous nature.
IMG4	c_sat3.gif
.
QUESTION	The Jovian Planets are the four gaseous planets and consist of the fifth through the eighth planets.  Which planet is a Jovian Planet?
INCORRECT_ANS1	Venus is one of the Terrestrial Planets.
IMG1	c_ven1.gif
CORRECT_ANS	Jupiter is one of the Jovian Planets.  Saturn, Uranus and Neptune are also Jovian Planets.
IMG2	c_jup3.gif
INCORRECT_ANS2	Pluto is not one of the four Jovian Planets because it is not gaseous.
IMG3	c_plu1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS3	Earth is one of the four Terrestrial Planets.
IMG4	c_ear1.gif
.
QUESTION	Which planet is one of the four Terrestrial Planets and also has an enormous circular basin on its surface called the Caloris Basin?
INCORRECT_ANS1	Earth is one of the Terrestrial Planets but it does not have the Caloris Basin on its surface.
IMG1	c_ear1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS2	Neptune is one of the Jovian Planets.
IMG2	c_nep2.gif
CORRECT_ANS	Mercury has a large circular basin like those found on the moon called the Caloris Basin.
IMG3	c_mer1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS3	Mars is one of the Terrestrial Planets but it is not the one with the Caloris Basin on its surface.
IMG4	c_mar1.gif
.
QUESTION	This planet has many volcanoes and a fractured surface.  Its atmosphere is 96% carbon dioxide and its surface temperature is more than twice as hot as the Earth's.
CORRECT_ANS	Venus has an unstable surface and it is very hot.  It also has clouds made up of sulfuric acid.
IMG1	c_ven1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS1	Halley's Comet is not a planet.
IMG2	c_hai2.gif
INCORRECT_ANS2	Jupiter is a gaseous planet without volcanoes.
IMG3	c_jup1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS3	Neptune is a gaseous planet without volcanoes. 
IMG4	c_nep2.gif
.
QUESTION	This planet has a diameter of 12756 km and the highest point on its surface is the tip of Mount Everest.  Its atmosphere is made up of 21% oxygen.
INCORRECT_ANS1	Saturn's atmosphere contains virtually no oxygen.  Saturn's atmosphere contains mostly hydrogen (97%).
IMG1	c_sat1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS2	Uranus has a diameter of 51118 km.  Almost 4 times the size of the planet with Mount Everest.
IMG2	c_ura1.gif
CORRECT_ANS	Earth's atmosphere has the oxygen that humans require to breathe.
IMG3	c_ear2.gif
INCORRECT_ANS3	Mars is smaller and its atmosphere is 95% carbon dioxide.
IMG4	c_mar1.gif
.
QUESTION	Which planet is larger than Mars but smaller than Earth?
INCORRECT_ANS1	Jupiter is many times larger than Earth. 
IMG1	c_jup1.gif
CORRECT_ANS	Venus is almost twice the size of Mars but it is just barely smaller than Earth.  Venus is 12104 km in diameter.
IMG2	c_ven1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS2	Neptune is larger than Earth.
IMG3	c_nep1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS3	Saturn is a planet that is larger than Earth.
IMG4	c_sat3.gif
.
QUESTION	Which planet has one natural satellite called the "Moon"?
CORRECT_ANS	Earth is the third planet from the Sun and only has one natural orbiting body called the "Moon".
IMG1	c_ear1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS1	The Moon does not orbit Uranus.
IMG2	c_ura1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS2	Earth would be considered a natural satellite of the Sun.
IMG3	c_sun1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS3	Pluto does have a natural satellite called Charon.  Although this is a moon, it is not the "Moon".
IMG4	c_plu1.gif
.
QUESTION	This planet ranks as the third smallest planet.  It is a little hotter than Earth but not because it is closer to the Sun.
CORRECT_ANS	Mars is the third smallest planet and is hotter than Earth due to its lack of protective atmosphere. 
IMG1	c_mar1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS1	Jupiter is the largest planet.
IMG2	c_jup1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS2	A comet is not one of the planets.
IMG3	c_hai1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS3	Saturn is a Jovian Planet that ranks second to largest.
IMG4	c_sat1.gif
.
QUESTION	This gas giant is 11 times bigger than Earth and 20% larger than Saturn.  It has a diameter of 142800km.
INCORRECT_ANS1	Venus is not one of the gas giants.
IMG1	c_ven1.gif
CORRECT_ANS	Jupiter is a gas giant and the largest planet in the Solar System.  Two of Jupiter's moons, Io and Europa can be seen in the picture.
IMG2	c_jup1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS2	Pluto is the smallest planet.
IMG3	c_plu1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS3	The Earth is not a gas giant.
IMG4	c_ear1.gif
.
QUESTION	This planet is the fourth largest planet and has a larger mass than Uranus.  It is nicknamed "The Mystic".
CORRECT_ANS	Neptune is smaller than Uranus but it is larger in mass.  It will actually be the furthest planet from the Sun until 1999 when Pluto again becomes furthest.
IMG1	c_nep1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS1	Halley's Comet is not a planet.
IMG2	c_hai2.gif
INCORRECT_ANS2	Jupiter is the largest planet.
IMG3	c_jup1.gif
INCORRECT_ANS3	Pluto is the smallest planet. 
IMG4	c_plu1.gif
.
